    "spectrophotometer",
    "Fig. 4 shows the X-ray diffraction pattern of silver nanoparticles synthesized by C. epithymum. The pattern indicates that the nanoparticles are spherical, with peaks at 2θ values of 27.84°, 32.23°, and 46.18° Furthermore, the XRD pattern corresponds to the reference pattern (JCPDS No. 04–0783) for silver nanoparticles. The provided formula can be utilized to calculate the crystallite size of these nanoparticles:D=kλβcosθFig. 4Analysis of the X-ray diffraction spectrum (XRD): It was found that the synthesized silver nanoparticles have high purity and are crystallized, as evidenced by the presence of strong and distinct peaks.Fig. 4"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": 0,
      "title": "Prepare Cuscuta epithymum aqueous extract",
      "instruction": "Weigh 5 g of dried Cuscuta epithymum powder, place it in a sterilized screw‑cap bottle, add 100 mL distilled water, heat the mixture in a water bath at 80–90 °C for 45 min, filter through Whatman No. 2 filter paper, and store the filtrate at the appropriate temperature until use.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 1,
      "title": "Perform agar disk diffusion antibacterial assay",
      "instruction": "Prepare sterile nutrient agar, pour 10 mL into each Petri dish, allow to solidify, inoculate the surface with the test bacteria, load sterile 6 mm discs (Pad tan Teb) with 10, 20, 40, and 80 ppm of the synthesized silver nanoparticles, autoclave the loaded discs, place them on the inoculated agar, incubate the plates at 37 °C for 24 h, then measure the inhibition‑zone diameters in millimetres.",
      "substeps": [
        {
          "instruction": "Prepare and sterilize nutrient agar medium.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Dispense 10 mL of molten agar into each Petri dish and let solidify.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Spread the bacterial culture uniformly over the solidified agar surface.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Place sterile 6 mm discs (Pad tan Teb) into separate sterile tubes.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Add 10 ppm AgNP solution to one set of discs, 20 ppm to a second set, 40 ppm to a third set, and 80 ppm to a fourth set.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Autoclave the loaded discs to ensure sterility.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Position the autoclaved, loaded discs onto the inoculated agar plates.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Incubate the plates at 37 °C for 24 hours.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "After incubation, measure the diameter of each inhibition zone in millimetres.",
          "title": ""
        }
      ],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    }
